From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:25:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] xmllite: answer IsDefault, instead of a stub.

IsDefault says whether the attribute the reader is on came from a default
that a DTD declared.  None does here: an internal subset is not parsed, and
a document with one fails, and an external one is never read.  So FALSE is
the answer, as it was, without the FIXME Office's readers set off twelve
thousand times while Word starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit e3b1eaf04cb0f2a0a2e21a0092ba1aac3ad2055d)

diff --git a/dlls/xmllite/reader.c b/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
index ce465822fba..88cc59e5e42 100644
--- a/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
+++ b/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
@@ -3429,9 +3429,11 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI xmlreader_GetBaseUri(IXmlReader* iface,
     return E_NOTIMPL;
 }
 
+/* Whether the current attribute came from a default a DTD declares.  None does here: an internal subset is
+ * not parsed, and a document with one fails in reader_parse_dtd, and an external one is never read. */
 static BOOL WINAPI xmlreader_IsDefault(IXmlReader* iface)
 {
-    FIXME("%p: stub\n", iface);
+    TRACE("%p\n", iface);
     return FALSE;
 }
 
